  "id": "strong-methods",
  "term": "strong methods",
  "definition": "In this learning context, strong methods are teaching approaches that effectively build understanding of concepts at scales that are hard to perceive directly. The packet describes them as using carefully structured analogies, progressive alignment of scale information, and active prediction with immediate feedback to improve reasoning.",
